# TypeScript And Aliases

- All application code must be written in TypeScript (`.ts` / `.tsx`).
- Avoid creating new JavaScript source files (`.js` / `.jsx`) in `src`.
- Use one path alias per module root in `tsconfig.json` (e.g. `@api`, `@services`). Do not add duplicate entries such as `@api` and `@api/*` for the same root.
- Import from each layer's `index.ts` barrel (`@api`, `@services`, `@components`, `@templates`, `@i18n`, `@atoms`, etc.) when crossing layers (e.g. `pages` → `@components`, `molecules` → `@atoms`, `lib` → `@services`).
- Avoid deep relative paths like `../../../` when a barrel alias exists for that cross-layer import.
- Within the same package root folder, prefer relative imports to avoid circular dependencies through the barrel. This includes:
  - `services/*` importing sibling files under `services/`
  - `api/*` importing sibling files under `api/`
  - `ui/components/*` importing another folder under `ui/components/` (e.g. `../admin/...`)
  - `ui/templates/*` importing another folder under `ui/templates/` (e.g. `../dashboard/...`)
  - `ui/molecules/*` importing sibling molecules (e.g. `../Card/Card`)
  - co-located files in the same component folder (e.g. `./useChatAutoScroll`, `../Input`)

## Example

```ts
// ✅ cross-layer — use barrel alias
import { useAuth, AuthProvider } from "@services";
import type { UserRole } from "@api";
import { AdminPromptDefaultsPage } from "@components";
import { Icon } from "@atoms";

// ✅ same package root — relative avoids barrel cycles
import { AdminPromptTemplatesPanel } from "../admin/AdminPromptTemplatesPanel";
import { DashboardSectionTitle } from "../dashboard/DashboardSectionTitle";
import { apiRequest } from "../../http/apiClient";

// ❌ cross-layer via relative path
import { AuthProvider } from "../services/auth/AuthProvider";
import { Icon } from "../../atoms";
```
